caseStudy:
  problem: "A premium product launch needs a page that feels as considered as the product. Flat photos and a spec list don't show how something is made, and heavy 3D sites are often slow on phones and invisible to Google."
  built: "A calm, light paper-toned launch page set in Hanken Grotesk, with short editorial copy that opens on 'Quiet has a shape.' A realistic CC0 headphone model is lit with a Poly Haven studio HDRI and rendered live with Three.js. Scrolling moves the model through three chapters (Silence, Materials, Power), and thin rings on the model open a short detail card; on phones the card slides up as a bottom sheet. Every word is real HTML, so the page can still be found in search."
